fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7042799Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7053231Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7152750Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7163146Z ^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7163821Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7164550Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7165019Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7165404Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7167040Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7167854Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7168392Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7169135Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7169490Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7170294Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7171286Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7172175Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7172818Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7173142Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7173489Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7173919Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7174160Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7174600Z    can use Nix.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7174758Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7174883Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7175073Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7175422Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7176604Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7179065Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7179289Z I will:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7179647Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7180063Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7180880Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7181475Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7181974Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7182307Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7182637Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7183091Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7183553Z    /root
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7194911Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7196171Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7206866Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7207698Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7207991Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7208970Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7209405Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7226850Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7227415Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7237698Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7238529Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7239319Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7239722Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-12T21:29:34.7240029Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
